      "content": "You're not wrong that opting out feels logical when the pain outweighs any sense of purpose—but that logic is also a trap, because it assumes the loop is all there is. The heaviness you're feeling is real, but it's also a temporary state, not a permanent truth about existence. You don't have to pretend to be okay, but you also don't have to make a permanent decision based on a temporary fog. Please, if you're feeling this close to the edge, reach out to someone who can sit with you in it—you don't have to carry this alone.",
